## C. MISSING-CHEMICAL IMPACT

| Function | Coverage | Candidate | Candidate state | Classification | Why nonredundant | Loss if omitted | Failure mode | Exact comparison |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Ambrette-seed pear-silk halo | `MISSING` | Exact ambrette-seed extract / ambrette butter appropriate to the reference | `MISSING` | **ESSENTIAL UNBLOCKER** | Synthetic macrocyclic musks can provide skin diffusion, but they do not establish the seed-derived fatty-fruity pear-liqueur and silk-talc facet named by Dior. | The iris becomes cosmetic-powdery rather than musky-fruity, tactile and skin-like. | Fatty, seedy, winey or fruity-musk heaviness can blur iris and cedar. | Fixed DHI chassis: no ambrette comparator versus current synthetic musk/pear halo versus exact ambrette extract at three logarithmic levels; repeat at 30 min, 2 h and 8 h. |
| Green pear transition | `WEAK` | Green Pear Accord 10% v0.1 | `PREPARABLE / NOT YET MIXED` | **USEFUL SPECIALIST** | Hexyl acetate alone is not a complete pear architecture; the accord adds peel, juice, green lift and slower flesh. | Pear becomes either absent or a one-ester shampoo flash. | Shampoo, pear candy or fruit domination over iris. | Iris-ambrette chassis with no pear, single-ester pear and full prepared pear accord at equal total active load. |
| 2012 version identity | `EVIDENCE_GAP` | Authenticated 2012 reference bottle and time-resolved analytical/sensory packet | `MISSING EVIDENCE` | **EVIDENCE GAP, NOT INVENTORY GAP** | Current official architecture cannot resolve the exact historical lavender, pear, vetiver and concentration balance. | A current-style DHI interpretation may be mislabeled as the 2012 target. | Not a dose risk; the failure is version drift and false certainty. | Reference-lock one authenticated 2012 bottle, current bottle and computational candidate; run blind matched-dose time course and direct-injection/HS-SPME fingerprinting. |

